Imports

import java.io.*;
Imports classes for input/output operations.
You specifically use PrintWriter from here to send response data to the browser.

import javax.servlet.*;
Gives access to core servlet classes like:

ServletException
RequestDispatcher (not used here, but should be)

import javax.servlet.http.*;
Required for HTTP-specific servlet handling.
Provides:
HttpServlet
HttpServletRequest
HttpServletResponse

Class Declaration
public class CalcServlet extends HttpServlet {
You are creating a servlet named CalcServlet.
It extends HttpServlet, meaning:
It can handle HTTP requests (GET, POST, etc.)

doPost Method
@Override
protected void doPost(HttpServletRequest req, HttpServletResponse res)
        throws ServletException, IOException {
This method runs when a POST request is sent to the servlet.
req → contains client data (form inputs)
res → used to send response back

Setting Response Type
res.setContentType("text/html");
Tells browser: “I’m sending HTML content.”
Without this, browser may misinterpret output.

Getting Output Stream
PrintWriter out = res.getWriter();
Creates a writer to send text back to the client.
Everything you out.println() becomes part of the webpage.
Getting Form Parameters

String num1Str = req.getParameter("num1");
String num2Str = req.getParameter("num2");
String op = req.getParameter("operation");
Reads values sent from HTML form.

These are always strings, even if user enters numbers.
"num1", "num2", "operation" must match form field names.
Null Check
if (num1Str == null || num2Str == null || op == null) {
    out.println("<h3>Error: Missing input values!</h3>");
    return;
}

Checks if any input is missing.
If missing:
prints error
return; stops further execution

Try Block (Parsing & Logic)
try {
Used to catch invalid number formats.

Converting Strings to Integers
int num1 = Integer.parseInt(num1Str);
int num2 = Integer.parseInt(num2Str);

Converts input strings into integers.
If user enters "abc" → throws NumberFormatException.

Result Variable
int result = 0;
Stores calculation result.
Initialized to avoid compile error.

Switch Case (Core Logic)
switch (op) {
Chooses operation based on input.
Addition
case "add": result = num1 + num2; break;
Adds numbers.
Subtraction
case "sub": result = num1 - num2; break;
Multiplication
case "mul": result = num1 * num2; break;
Division
case "div":
if (num2 != 0) {
    result = num1 / num2;
}
Prevents division by zero.
else {
    out.println("<h3>Error: Division by zero!</h3>");
    return;
}
If divisor is zero:
print error
stop execution

Default Case
default:
    out.println("<h3>Error: Invalid operation!</h3>");
    return;
Handles unexpected operation input.

Display Result
out.println("<h2>Result: " + result + "</h2>");
Sends result as HTML to browser.

Catch Block
} catch (NumberFormatException e) {
Runs if conversion fails (invalid number input)
out.println("<h3>Error: Please enter valid numbers!</h3>");
Displays error message

Closing Braces
}
}
End of try-catch
End of doPost
End of class
